In other words, the set of isomorphism classes of first order thickenings $i : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}')$ over $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{B}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {B})$ endowed with an isomorphism $\mathcal{G} \to \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(i^\sharp )$ of $\mathcal{O}$-modules.